<GuideLayout slug="watchlist" updated="2026-11-21">
  <h2>Why keep a watchlist</h2>
  <p>Most players trade the same handful of items over and over: the materials for their profession, what they farm, a piece of gear they're saving up for. Looking each one up every day gets old. The <a href="/watchlist">watchlist</a> keeps them in one place with this hour's prices, how they've moved over the past week, and a flag when one drops to the price you want to pay.</p>
  <p>There's no account and no sign-up. Your list is saved in your own browser.</p>

  <h2>Adding items</h2>
  <p>Click the star next to any item on <a href="/prices">Auction prices</a>, <a href="/flips">Vendor flips</a> or an <a href="/item">item price page</a>. Starred items appear on the watchlist and also at the top of the <a href="/">home page</a>, for the auction house you've picked, so you see them as soon as you open the site.</p>
  <p class="tip"><b>Good things to watch:</b> the materials you buy for your profession, what you farm to sell, the crafted goods you sell, and gear you're saving for.</p>

  <h2>Reading each row</h2>
  <ul class="gems">
    <li><b>Lowest</b> and <b>Market</b>: this hour's cheapest listing, and the market price (the average of the cheapest 10% on sale). <b>Listed</b> is how many are for sale.</li>
    <li><b>7 days</b>: how this hour's market price compares with the market price about a week ago. A steady fall can mean a farming spot got popular; a steady rise, that a recipe using the item became the thing to craft.</li>
    <li><b>Sold/day</b>: an estimate of how many sell per day on your house, from the past week's hourly snapshots.</li>
    <li><b>Cheaper elsewhere</b>: another auction house in your ruleset where the item is at least 5% cheaper. Remember Alliance and Horde can only trade across factions through Blackwater.</li>
    <li><b>Not listed</b>: nobody is selling it on your house this hour.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Target prices</h2>
  <p>In the <b>Flag at or below</b> column, type a price in the gold, silver and copper boxes, just like on the in-game auction house. Whenever the item's lowest listing is at that price or cheaper, the row is highlighted as <b>At your target</b>, here and on the home page. Clear all three boxes to remove the target.</p>
  <p>A good target is a little below the usual market price: check the 30-day chart on the item's page and pick a price it reaches on its cheaper days. Then buy when the flag shows, instead of paying whatever the market wants on the day you need it.</p>

  <h2>Taking it to another device</h2>
  <p>Because the list lives in your browser, it doesn't follow you to your phone or another computer by itself. Click <b>Copy share link</b> and open that link on the other device: it shows the shared list with a button to <b>Add to my watchlist</b>. The same link works for sending a list to a friend or your guild's crafters.</p>
  <p>Clearing your browser's site data deletes the watchlist, so keep a share link if you've built a long one.</p>
</GuideLayout>
